## Why LATIFY Is the Most Important Trial in This Set

The first three trials were ovarian cancer. Important. But ovarian cancer affects ~20,000 US patients per year.

**Lung cancer affects 230,000+.** Non-small cell lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer death. IO therapy (pembrolizumab, nivolumab, atezolizumab) has transformed NSCLC outcomes — but only for a subset of patients.

The STK11/KEAP1-altered subset — approximately **20–30% of NSCLC** — is systematically IO-resistant. These are patients who get pembrolizumab, don't respond, and progress. They're the patients the KEYTRUDA PROBLEM describes in lung cancer.

**LATIFY targets exactly those patients.** Ceralasertib + durvalumab for patients where IO already failed. If CrisPRO can identify:
1. STK11/KEAP1-altered patients before treatment (NGS panel — available today)
2. Recommend ceralasertib + durvalumab instead of pembrolizumab monotherapy
3. Avoid the futile IO course with its associated toxicity ($150K, irAEs)

That is a **Merck conversation** ("some of your Keytruda non-responders could have been identified upfront"). That is an **AstraZeneca conversation** ("ceralasertib + durvalumab should be first-line for STK11-loss, not rescue therapy"). That is a **payer conversation** ("we can identify the non-responders before they spend $150K").

